{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_1b83494a3c9f1080753e6be3c0097431b023be508ea5f95b750d60afeb35020b", "title": "World Fellowship Center", "text": "The World Fellowship Center is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization and retreat/conference center located in Albany, New Hampshire, United States. It is open from late June to approximately Labor Day weekend, with a few workshops and other events taking place before or afterwards. Nestled at the southeastern edge of the White Mountain National Forest, east of Mount Chocorua off Route 16 in Albany, it currently comprises approximately 455 acre , including a conference room and dining lodge, nature trail, soccer field, several cabins, campsites and additional lodging facilities, as well as boating and swimming access to a large pond. At capacity it can host over 200 guests and features speakers, groups, organizations, activists and entertainers from around the world.", "score": 18.2298}, {"id": "hp_doc_c66ba94a4d4abc059c99cea92fe897789bbc8dbbe75d910e93296123570321c9", "title": "Billy Wilson (academic)", "text": "Billy Wilson (born October 4, 1958) is the president of Oral Roberts University in Tulsa, Oklahoma. Prior to his election as president of Oral Roberts University, Wilson served as the vice chairman for the ORU Board of Trustees. He has also served as the executive director for the International Center for Spiritual Renewal in Cleveland, Tennessee and the chair and executive director of the Empowered 21 Initiative. In addition, Wilson has served on various boards and committees, including the Mission America Coalition (Lausanne USA) Facilitation Committee, the Pentecostal World Fellowship Advisory Board, and the International Christian Embassy Jerusalem.", "score": 12.408}, {"id": "hp_doc_88b58d2c703512e5ce9425f7e0ddf633482a85d0ca11ec5ae86a1ebe110b83ab", "title": "CJFY-FM", "text": "CJFY-FM is a Canadian radio station in Miramichi, New Brunswick broadcasting on 96.5 MHz. The station broadcasts a Christian music format and is owned by Miramichi Fellowship Center, Inc. CJFY has been on the air since 2004, originally at 107.5 FM. Since 2005, CJFY has also been operating a rebroadcaster at 107.7 MHz in Blackville.", "score": 12.3607}], "remaining_searches": 2}
